    <p>In first two graphs, respondents rated their answer from 1 (strong disagreement) to 5 (strong agreement). 76.6% agreed that they made close friends in the program. All engineering classes at UW are placed into cohorts: you take the same courses and co-op sequence as the rest of your cohort for most of your degree. The cohort system is often touted as a key benefit over non-eng programs: the people around you really make the experience!</p>
